WEBVTT

00:00:19.703 --> 00:00:23.873
It's The Futurama Holiday
Spectacular brought to you by...

00:00:27.628 --> 00:00:29.712
Ah, the Xmas season.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.798
Who wants a delicious
unshelled nut?

00:00:31.882 --> 00:00:34.008
Ooh, I'll have one.

00:00:39.389 --> 00:00:41.349
It's "nut" so good.

00:00:43.101 --> 00:00:46.729
What's wrong, Fry? Are you
regretting another wasted year?

00:00:47.189 --> 00:00:49.273
I don't know.
Something about Xmas

00:00:49.358 --> 00:00:50.942
just doesn't feel
like Christmas.

00:00:52.736 --> 00:00:55.863
Santa's coming!
Initiate defenses!

00:01:05.374 --> 00:01:08.334
God rest
ye merry gentlemen

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.169
in peace.

00:01:14.258 --> 00:01:18.427
Can someone please explain how
you celebrate this crazy holiday?

00:01:18.679 --> 00:01:19.929
Preferably in song.

00:01:21.974 --> 00:01:25.059
It's the violentest
season of the year

00:01:25.769 --> 00:01:29.021
When Kringle-bot come
dispensing mugs of Xmas fear

00:01:29.773 --> 00:01:32.316
Sugar plummy visions will be dancing in your head

00:01:32.401 --> 00:01:35.361
When I cane you
from the comfort of my sled

00:01:36.363 --> 00:01:39.031
On Xmas Eve,
we don our gay apparel

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:43.077
Kevlar vests, asbestos stockings and a barrel

00:01:43.161 --> 00:01:46.539
And if Grandma's Xmas fruitcake
finally reaches critical mass

00:01:46.623 --> 00:01:49.208
It can be re-gifted
straight to Santa's ass

00:01:51.795 --> 00:01:55.256
But the ornamental armaments
are merely superficial

00:01:55.465 --> 00:01:58.718
The tinsel and the trappings
are just icing on the missile

00:01:59.136 --> 00:02:03.306
The one thing that you need to
make your Xmas Day splendiferous

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:07.351
Is a pine tree
A pine tree that's coniferous

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:11.230
We have to have a pine tree
that's coniferous

00:02:12.316 --> 00:02:13.649
You're welcome.

00:02:14.651 --> 00:02:18.321
You know, Santa may have killed
Scruffy, but he makes a good point.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:21.073
What we need is an
old-fashioned pine tree.

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:22.366
Cram it, Virginia.

00:02:22.451 --> 00:02:25.953
Pine trees have been
extinct for over 800 years.

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:28.080
Professor,
maybe there's some way

00:02:28.165 --> 00:02:30.124
to bring the pine
trees back to life.

00:02:30.208 --> 00:02:32.084
Like we did with
the barking snakes.

00:02:34.004 --> 00:02:35.922
Pine trees aren't
barking snakes.

00:02:36.006 --> 00:02:38.883
They won't just turn up
in a salad at Olive Garden.

00:02:38.967 --> 00:02:43.304
But there is one hope and,
as usual, it's Norwegian.

00:02:57.444 --> 00:02:58.444
Behold!

00:02:58.695 --> 00:03:01.822
The Svalbard
Global Seed Vault.

00:03:01.949 --> 00:03:07.119
Since 2008, the vault has preserved
seeds of every known plant species,

00:03:07.204 --> 00:03:08.829
in case of extinction.

00:03:08.914 --> 00:03:10.665
And I brought
a few seeds of my own.

00:03:13.043 --> 00:03:16.295
Halt! What's your business
pokey-poking about the seed vault?

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:19.340
Guardian of mankind's precious
botanical heritage there?

00:03:19.424 --> 00:03:22.301
We just want to come in
and rummage about a bit.

00:03:22.386 --> 00:03:25.054
Oh, so... Okay.

00:03:25.973 --> 00:03:28.557
Yo, ABBA,
what's that next door?

00:03:29.685 --> 00:03:32.144
That's the Germ
Warfare Repository.

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:33.396
It's so close.

00:03:33.563 --> 00:03:36.649
Is there any chance
of cross-contamination?

00:03:36.858 --> 00:03:38.359
No.

00:03:40.195 --> 00:03:41.862
Now, your pine trees
were all chopped down

00:03:41.947 --> 00:03:44.991
to make emergency toilet paper
during the Fifty-Year Squirts.

00:03:45.075 --> 00:03:47.410
Lucky the seeds have been
preserved here in the vault there.

00:03:47.577 --> 00:03:49.328
What's that splork on them?

00:03:49.579 --> 00:03:51.747
It's not germs, is it?

00:03:51.832 --> 00:03:52.832
No.

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:07.680
Now that's a tree
worth chopping down.

00:04:07.764 --> 00:04:10.433
Indeed,
'tis a lovely tree.

00:04:10.559 --> 00:04:13.978
'Twill truly be my
finest Xmas ever.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.232
That's what my
poll numbers need.

00:04:18.316 --> 00:04:21.610
Happy voters enjoying
some holiday cheer.

00:04:21.695 --> 00:04:25.948
As your vice-president, I
order you to steal that tree.

00:04:27.617 --> 00:04:29.285
My fellow Earthicans,

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:32.830
welcome to the annual White
House Xmas-tree lighting,

00:04:32.956 --> 00:04:36.167
brought to you by
Gunderson's Nuts.

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:37.376
Gunderson!

00:04:49.473 --> 00:04:52.516
Oh, no! Could the seed have been contaminated

00:04:52.601 --> 00:04:54.852
by a virus from
the germ vault?

00:04:54.978 --> 00:04:56.479
Yeah, I suppose.

00:04:56.563 --> 00:04:59.899
Wait. This could be a good
thing. That weaponized virus

00:04:59.983 --> 00:05:02.735
made the sickly, little tree
grow big and strong.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.667
Wait. This could be
a good thing.

00:05:18.752 --> 00:05:20.336
Reforestation has begun.

00:05:23.006 --> 00:05:24.673
Geez, with these...

00:05:44.861 --> 00:05:47.071
Arguably, this could
be a good thing.

00:05:47.155 --> 00:05:50.032
The planet has returned
to its primeval state.

00:05:50.117 --> 00:05:53.619
Earth is just the way it was
before the white man came.

00:05:53.703 --> 00:05:55.871
Good news.

00:05:56.039 --> 00:05:58.791
All these pine trees are
fighting global warming

00:05:58.875 --> 00:06:00.292
by producing oxygen.

00:06:00.377 --> 00:06:01.460
Happy now, Gore?

00:06:01.545 --> 00:06:02.586
Yeah.

00:06:02.671 --> 00:06:05.464
But I'd be happier if
I had a set of lungs.

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:10.052
Wait a second. Oxygen levels
are rising too rapidly.

00:06:10.262 --> 00:06:14.640
10%, 20%, 60%.

00:06:14.766 --> 00:06:16.392
As long as it
doesn't hit 70.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.227
80%.

00:06:18.395 --> 00:06:21.105
You know, I don't recall having
done anything for a while,

00:06:21.189 --> 00:06:23.607
but I still feel
I deserve a smoke.

00:06:26.027 --> 00:06:28.737
Hey, cool.
The air is on fire.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:35.995
Ho, ho, ho.

00:06:36.079 --> 00:06:37.788
Everyone's dead.

00:06:37.873 --> 00:06:42.751
Stay tuned for another tale
of holiday hilarity.

00:06:46.214 --> 00:06:49.008
Now back to
the Gunderson's Nuts

00:06:49.134 --> 00:06:51.927
Holiday Spectacular
featuring Futurama.

00:06:52.304 --> 00:06:55.014
Okay, crew.
Xmas break is over.

00:06:55.098 --> 00:06:58.267
It's time to destroy these
gifts we forgot to deliver.

00:06:58.351 --> 00:06:59.810
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:06:59.895 --> 00:07:02.354
How come we get off for every dumb human holiday,

00:07:02.439 --> 00:07:04.523
but not for
robot holidays?

00:07:04.608 --> 00:07:06.567
Oh, Lord.
Not Robanukah.

00:07:06.651 --> 00:07:08.569
I'm talking about Robanukah,

00:07:08.653 --> 00:07:11.906
the holiest six and a half
weeks in the robot calendar.

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:16.452
That's just a fake holiday you make
up every year to get out of work.

00:07:16.536 --> 00:07:18.078
Yeah. If it's real,

00:07:18.163 --> 00:07:20.956
how come there's no song that
explains how to celebrate it?

00:07:21.041 --> 00:07:22.541
Because there is.

00:07:22.792 --> 00:07:24.668
Hit it.
Hit what?

00:07:24.836 --> 00:07:26.962
I placed instruments
under your seats.

00:07:27.047 --> 00:07:28.964
Play them or I'll break them over your heads.

00:07:30.884 --> 00:07:33.802
Robanukah may sound
as if it's Jewish

00:07:34.221 --> 00:07:37.932
But its ancient-sounding
customs are exceptionally newish

00:07:38.141 --> 00:07:41.101
So take a hearty swallow
from your robo-Kiddush cup

00:07:41.186 --> 00:07:43.812
Which will give me time
to quickly make them up

00:07:45.315 --> 00:07:47.816
Do you spin
a dreidel made from clay?

00:07:48.568 --> 00:07:51.654
Mine is called a droid-el and
it's rigged to make you pay

00:07:53.782 --> 00:07:56.450
Do you eat these yummy,
tin-wrapped chocolate coins?

00:07:56.993 --> 00:08:00.079
Better. We got fem-bots
with illegal five-speed groins

00:08:00.163 --> 00:08:02.998
Shalom, Ruth and Esther.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.501
Why with the music
so loud?

00:08:05.585 --> 00:08:08.921
Would it kill him to turn up
the heat a little in here?

00:08:09.506 --> 00:08:12.424
By far, the most
important thing is oil

00:08:12.676 --> 00:08:15.970
To keep the lamp light burning
or to help the latkes broil

00:08:16.054 --> 00:08:19.932
No, we pour the holy lubricant
out from this sacred vessel

00:08:20.016 --> 00:08:23.018
into this blessed
pit so they can wrestle

00:08:23.353 --> 00:08:26.730
The extra made-up touch
that makes Robanukah so special

00:08:26.815 --> 00:08:30.276
is the oil in which the
nasty fem-bots wrestle

00:08:30.443 --> 00:08:33.529
We shall now begin the
traditional oil wrestling.

00:08:33.613 --> 00:08:37.408
Will the referee bring out the
ceremonial cruse of petroleum oil?

00:08:39.244 --> 00:08:41.120
Thank you, Abraham.

00:08:41.329 --> 00:08:44.373
Not in the hair, please.
I just had it did.

00:08:48.044 --> 00:08:49.211
Oh, no.

00:08:49.296 --> 00:08:51.880
These broads are supposed to
wrestle for six and a half weeks,

00:08:51.965 --> 00:08:55.134
but there's only enough petroleum
oil for four and a half weeks.

00:08:56.803 --> 00:08:58.178
We're still
getting paid, right?

00:08:58.263 --> 00:09:00.723
I told you it's an audition!

00:09:00.807 --> 00:09:04.184
Bender, four and a half weeks of
oil wrestling sounds like plenty.

00:09:04.269 --> 00:09:07.021
This isn't
a lousy reform Robanukah.

00:09:07.105 --> 00:09:09.023
We need more petroleum oil!

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:17.448
I got me some whale oil,
some squirrel oil.

00:09:17.532 --> 00:09:20.284
Not kosher!
It has to be petroleum oil!

00:09:20.368 --> 00:09:23.912
Do you not give a damn about the
hallowed traditions of Robanukah?

00:09:23.997 --> 00:09:25.622
I reckon I do not.

00:09:25.749 --> 00:09:28.083
Anyways, Earth done run out
of petroleum oil.

00:09:29.627 --> 00:09:31.295
I tried to warn you.

00:09:31.379 --> 00:09:33.839
One unit of free,
limitless solar power, please.

00:09:39.095 --> 00:09:41.764
That'll be,
I don't know, 10 bucks.

00:09:42.599 --> 00:09:44.808
Can you make change
for a Nobel Prize?

00:09:45.226 --> 00:09:48.479
Man, can't we just make
more petroleum oil?

00:09:48.605 --> 00:09:50.356
I'm afraid not, son.

00:09:50.607 --> 00:09:52.983
Petroleum only forms
when organic matter

00:09:53.068 --> 00:09:58.072
is subjected to intense pressure
for hundreds of millions of years.

00:09:58.281 --> 00:10:00.824
I can't wait that long.
I've got ADD.

00:10:00.909 --> 00:10:03.410
This is so unfair.

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:06.955
I don't wrestle dry, Bender.
I went to Vassar.

00:10:07.082 --> 00:10:10.834
Professor, I want you to look
these poor floozies in the eye

00:10:10.919 --> 00:10:13.629
and tell them their
oil-wrestling days are over.

00:10:22.013 --> 00:10:26.141
I suppose there could be a
minute quantity of petroleum left,

00:10:26.267 --> 00:10:28.560
but it would be insanely
deep within the Earth

00:10:28.645 --> 00:10:30.729
at pressures so
dangerously high...

00:10:32.148 --> 00:10:33.774
Let's go, already!

00:10:45.995 --> 00:10:48.205
Setting Bachman Turners
to Overdrive.

00:10:49.707 --> 00:10:53.085
We're getting pretty deep.
Look! Mole coffins.

00:11:04.931 --> 00:11:07.433
Oh, no.
We tunneled into a tunnel.

00:11:08.059 --> 00:11:11.478
What's that loud, boring sound
you'll hear when I stop talking?

00:11:12.355 --> 00:11:15.858
It's an albino humping worm.

00:11:16.025 --> 00:11:17.484
Why do they call it that?

00:11:18.778 --> 00:11:21.196
Because it doesn't
have any pigment.

00:11:25.201 --> 00:11:26.785
What's our depth, Captain?

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:28.871
Forty kilometers, 50.

00:11:28.955 --> 00:11:31.623
There must be petroleum oil
down here somewhere.

00:11:31.708 --> 00:11:33.292
Go deeper. Deeper!

00:11:33.376 --> 00:11:36.545
No, Bender. The ship can't
withstand this much pressure.

00:11:36.629 --> 00:11:39.715
Sometimes it falls apart
just sitting in the hangar.

00:11:39.799 --> 00:11:42.634
Professor, I've never asked for anything before,

00:11:42.969 --> 00:11:44.803
but seeing those
fem-bots glistening

00:11:44.888 --> 00:11:47.389
with oil means more
to me than life itself.

00:11:49.225 --> 00:11:53.395
Call me an old fool, but I believe
the Lord is speaking through you.

00:11:53.521 --> 00:11:55.814
Brace yourselves, everyone.

00:11:59.152 --> 00:12:00.235
One hundred kilometers.

00:12:01.821 --> 00:12:02.821
Two hundred.

00:12:02.906 --> 00:12:04.323
I hate to complain
about the heat,

00:12:04.407 --> 00:12:06.742
but the air conditioner's
on fire.

00:12:08.661 --> 00:12:10.370
My ice cream Manwich!

00:12:16.753 --> 00:12:18.212
What the hell
are we doing?

00:12:18.296 --> 00:12:22.424
We're all gonna die so this junkyard
golem can celebrate Robanukah.

00:12:23.134 --> 00:12:25.636
You vile racist.

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:28.013
Haven't my people
suffered enough?

00:12:28.264 --> 00:12:32.017
Now keep drilling for that
petroleum oil, you selfish cowards.

00:12:32.477 --> 00:12:35.354
Although, then again, I guess any
kind of oil would be just as...

00:12:36.564 --> 00:12:37.564
Not my fault.

00:12:41.277 --> 00:12:43.820
I am so great. Bender is great

00:12:43.988 --> 00:12:46.323
Bender, Bender, Bender

00:12:46.407 --> 00:12:48.033
Man, where'd the time go?

00:12:48.117 --> 00:12:50.786
Hey, you guys wanna...
Oh. Right.

00:12:53.581 --> 00:12:56.250
They turned
into petroleum oil.

00:12:57.001 --> 00:12:59.836
I thought they were selfish,
yet in the end,

00:12:59.921 --> 00:13:03.257
it turns out it was I
who thought they were selfish.

00:13:10.139 --> 00:13:12.558
Hey, ladies, I found some.
What the...

00:13:14.686 --> 00:13:16.270
There was only
enough petroleum oil

00:13:16.354 --> 00:13:18.355
for four and a half
weeks of oil wrestling,

00:13:18.439 --> 00:13:21.149
but it lasted
500 million years.

00:13:21.484 --> 00:13:23.151
It's a miracle.

00:13:23.987 --> 00:13:26.154
Happy Robanukah, everyone.

00:13:26.239 --> 00:13:30.701
Coming up next, more
thoughtful, interfaith hijinks.

00:13:34.289 --> 00:13:37.165
And now,
the unrelated conclusion.

00:13:42.505 --> 00:13:43.672
Hello, Fry.
Hey, Fry!

00:13:43.756 --> 00:13:44.881
How you doing?
What's up?

00:13:44.966 --> 00:13:47.718
LaBarbara, Hermes,
happy Kwanzaa.

00:13:47.802 --> 00:13:49.177
We brought a chocolate cake,

00:13:49.262 --> 00:13:51.847
but now I'm worried that
might be offensive in some way.

00:13:51.931 --> 00:13:53.432
Just sit down.

00:13:54.475 --> 00:13:56.935
Happy Kwanzaa,
brother men and sister men.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:59.771
Well, look at the cat
the cat dragged in.

00:13:59.856 --> 00:14:02.566
Kwanzaa tradition
encourages educational gifts.

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:05.193
So I brought Dwight
my book on mathketball.

00:14:05.653 --> 00:14:08.196
Whoa!
Let me see that.

00:14:09.741 --> 00:14:11.283
I'll sign it for you later.

00:14:11.367 --> 00:14:13.702
Man,
it's a cold one out there.

00:14:13.828 --> 00:14:15.120
Barbados Slim?

00:14:15.204 --> 00:14:16.788
Come in, Barbados.

00:14:16.873 --> 00:14:21.043
Look at yourself, all throbbing
and shirtless for the holiday.

00:14:21.336 --> 00:14:22.919
I hope you're
ready to celebrate.

00:14:23.004 --> 00:14:26.256
All night long, woman.

00:14:27.634 --> 00:14:30.302
I'm glad you all could be
here with my family.

00:14:30.386 --> 00:14:35.057
Kwanzaa traditions are quite
ancient, dating back over 1,000 years.

00:14:35.183 --> 00:14:36.475
Whoa!

00:14:36.559 --> 00:14:40.896
If only someone could tell us
more about these traditions.

00:14:41.564 --> 00:14:43.482
Oh, yeah.

00:14:43.566 --> 00:14:44.983
Hey, Kool-Aid's here.

00:14:45.068 --> 00:14:47.944
No, child. That's not
a made-up character.

00:14:48.029 --> 00:14:49.237
It's Kwanzaa-bot.

00:14:49.322 --> 00:14:52.032
And I'm gonna tell you all
how we celebrate Kwanzaa.

00:14:52.116 --> 00:14:54.076
Zoidberg, lay down a beat.

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:56.495
How about I just lay down?

00:15:00.083 --> 00:15:03.418
There's seven basic principles
that go to make up Kwanzaa

00:15:03.503 --> 00:15:07.047
So sit your asses down and have
some knowledge dropped upon ya

00:15:07.131 --> 00:15:08.757
Kujichagulia

00:15:08.841 --> 00:15:10.342
And Umoja.
And the rest!

00:15:10.426 --> 00:15:11.385
Now we get it

00:15:11.469 --> 00:15:13.762
Sit back down
There's gonna be a test

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:15.597
My favorite's Ujamaa

00:15:15.682 --> 00:15:17.307
Cooperative economics

00:15:17.392 --> 00:15:19.768
Yo, bulldog, I'm talking here
Put away the comics

00:15:21.145 --> 00:15:24.189
Ku'umba is another one
It stands for creativity

00:15:24.273 --> 00:15:27.901
Like the ever-changing nature
of my sexual proclivities

00:15:28.111 --> 00:15:31.154
I think there's one called Nia
but I don't speak Swahili

00:15:31.531 --> 00:15:34.658
Something about a pine tree
and an oil-wrestling deal-y?

00:15:34.742 --> 00:15:38.286
That's from Xmas and Robanukah
you plagiarizing lout

00:15:38.371 --> 00:15:41.707
Yeah, I'm kind of losing interest
here I best be rolling out

00:15:41.791 --> 00:15:45.127
But before I go,
the most important thing

00:15:45.503 --> 00:15:46.920
What's that, black Santa?

00:15:47.004 --> 00:15:50.424
You need seven Kwanzaa candles
that you light up every night

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:52.175
But they best be
made of beeswax

00:15:52.301 --> 00:15:53.969
or you all might
as well be white

00:15:54.345 --> 00:15:58.473
They must be made of beeswax
or we might as well be white

00:15:59.475 --> 00:16:01.560
Well, we got
no beeswax candles,

00:16:01.644 --> 00:16:05.313
but these scented regular
wax candles will do just fine.

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:08.692
Girl, those stink sticks are
for single women who take baths.

00:16:08.776 --> 00:16:11.528
If your Kwanzaa candles
ain't 100% beeswax,

00:16:11.654 --> 00:16:13.363
you bring shame
on your people.

00:16:13.448 --> 00:16:15.031
Well, now that won't do.

00:16:15.158 --> 00:16:16.992
Husband,
show a little Ku'umba

00:16:17.076 --> 00:16:19.536
and fetch some beeswax
before Kwanzaa ends.

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:22.038
Sweet candelabra of
La Habra, LaBarbara.

00:16:22.123 --> 00:16:23.999
Isn't this the last night
of Kwanzaa?

00:16:24.083 --> 00:16:25.751
Who the hell knows?

00:16:27.462 --> 00:16:30.672
Finally, a bee farm that's
open late on Kwanzaa.

00:16:30.882 --> 00:16:32.924
Madam, I need beeswax.

00:16:33.009 --> 00:16:35.302
You sure you don't need
a little honey, handsome?

00:16:35.386 --> 00:16:38.638
Maybe a taste of sweet nectar
straight from the hive?

00:16:39.932 --> 00:16:43.185
I just need some beeswax
to make Kwanzaa candles.

00:16:43.269 --> 00:16:44.770
Well, that's too darn bad.

00:16:44.854 --> 00:16:47.439
There ain't no beeswax
in the whole world.

00:16:47.523 --> 00:16:50.776
Oh, no. This could be
the year without a Kwanzaa,

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:53.528
like every year before 1966.

00:16:53.613 --> 00:16:55.405
The bees are
acting all crazy

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:58.158
like they been drinking
Tang and cough syrup,

00:16:58.242 --> 00:17:01.286
or as I call it,
my Friday night.

00:17:03.456 --> 00:17:04.623
My God.

00:17:04.874 --> 00:17:09.127
It's Colony Collapse Syndrome. The
bees are swarming with parasites.

00:17:09.295 --> 00:17:10.420
They're all dying.

00:17:10.505 --> 00:17:12.422
Yeah,
but what a way to go.

00:17:12.507 --> 00:17:15.634
"Die young, leave a pretty
corpse," that's what I say.

00:17:15.718 --> 00:17:17.427
You should say
something else.

00:17:17.512 --> 00:17:19.888
Wait. I know where
we can get beeswax.

00:17:19.972 --> 00:17:22.057
From those giant space bees
who nearly killed us,

00:17:22.141 --> 00:17:23.975
and we swore we'd
never go back there.

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:25.852
Let's go back there.

00:17:30.525 --> 00:17:32.025
To communicate
with the bees,

00:17:32.109 --> 00:17:34.736
we'll need to use
these trans-bumbleators.

00:17:34.821 --> 00:17:36.947
Bender,
say something in bee talk.

00:17:40.076 --> 00:17:43.119
I'm sorry, Bender. What do you
want me to put on the glass?

00:17:44.497 --> 00:17:46.581
Okay, if we survive.

00:17:55.091 --> 00:17:57.968
Something's wrong.
It's way too quiet.

00:17:58.094 --> 00:17:59.928
Like the deadly Prius.

00:18:01.389 --> 00:18:03.223
Ah,
here they come.

00:18:03.307 --> 00:18:05.559
They're in attack formation.
They're gonna kill us.

00:18:10.356 --> 00:18:11.648
That was weird.

00:18:11.732 --> 00:18:14.734
It's like the Jдgermeister
air show all over again.

00:18:19.615 --> 00:18:21.241
According to Google Hive,

00:18:21.325 --> 00:18:23.702
we are at the exact center
of the honeycomb.

00:18:24.412 --> 00:18:26.580
And there's a Jamba Juice 0.2 miles that way.

00:18:26.706 --> 00:18:28.957
Does that thing tell you
where the queen bee is?

00:18:29.041 --> 00:18:33.336
The big, fat, ugly,
compound-eyed, hairy-thoraxed...

00:18:33.421 --> 00:18:35.672
Don't be applying
your Eurocentric

00:18:35.756 --> 00:18:37.966
standards of
beauty to me, fool.

00:18:40.261 --> 00:18:41.720
What's with the
kamikaz-bees?

00:18:41.804 --> 00:18:44.055
Man, my hive's
been going buck-wild

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:47.642
since these blood-ganking
butt crabs moved in.

00:18:49.478 --> 00:18:51.271
Been there, done that.

00:18:51.355 --> 00:18:54.316
They're all infected,
just like the bees on Earth.

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:57.819
Brother-sucking parasites gone
and disrupted our hive mind.

00:18:57.904 --> 00:18:59.738
Now, instead of
working in harmony,

00:18:59.822 --> 00:19:02.240
my bees just talk
smack to each other.

00:19:02.325 --> 00:19:04.451
Are you all black
with yellow stripes

00:19:04.577 --> 00:19:06.703
or are you yellow
with black stripes?

00:19:06.829 --> 00:19:09.456
Yellow with
black stripes, man.

00:19:09.874 --> 00:19:12.667
Why don't you just move along?

00:19:12.835 --> 00:19:15.086
Let me ask you something,
you sting my wife?

00:19:15.171 --> 00:19:16.755
What kind of
buzzing question is that?

00:19:16.839 --> 00:19:20.091
Where do you get the wings
big enough to ask me that?

00:19:23.804 --> 00:19:27.599
Okay, gang. We have plenty of
beeswax. Let's get back to the ship.

00:19:27.683 --> 00:19:29.809
No, we are not
going anywhere.

00:19:29.894 --> 00:19:32.479
I can't abide all
this bee-on-bee conflict.

00:19:32.563 --> 00:19:35.565
It's time to African-Americanize these honeybees.

00:19:37.234 --> 00:19:41.488
Listen up, bees.
It's Kwanzaa, a time of Umoja.

00:19:41.572 --> 00:19:43.198
It means "unity".

00:19:45.368 --> 00:19:48.078
You have to learn to
work together again.

00:19:48.162 --> 00:19:50.622
The crazy
tablecloth man is right.

00:19:50.706 --> 00:19:53.208
It's time to set
aside our differences.

00:19:54.043 --> 00:19:56.169
Black stripe, yellow stripe.

00:19:56.337 --> 00:20:00.131
At the end of the day, we're just
a couple of darn talking space bees.

00:20:00.675 --> 00:20:02.342
Hey, forget about it.

00:20:02.426 --> 00:20:04.010
Come here
and give me a sting.

00:20:05.346 --> 00:20:09.307
Look. The spirit of Kwanzaa
is killing the parasites.

00:20:10.518 --> 00:20:11.518
Yuck!

00:20:11.602 --> 00:20:13.061
But, yay!

00:20:13.145 --> 00:20:14.896
Thank you, my human brother.

00:20:14.981 --> 00:20:18.066
Your message of unity
has touched our souls.

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:22.028
We are once again of
a single hive mind.

00:20:26.242 --> 00:20:28.034
Oh, yeah.

00:20:28.119 --> 00:20:29.619
Hurray! Kwanzaa-bot's
here to save...

00:20:30.746 --> 00:20:32.288
They killed him.

00:20:37.586 --> 00:20:40.046
Joyous Kwanzaa, everybody.

00:20:48.681 --> 00:20:52.058
Don't worry. The Futurama
crew will be back next year

00:20:52.143 --> 00:20:56.479
with all new episodes featuring
Bender, Leela and me, Al Gore,

00:20:56.564 --> 00:20:58.481
as Captain Lance Starman.

00:20:58.733 --> 00:21:02.068
And from all of us here at
Gunderson's Nuts, happy holidays.